module examples.err_dma_shared_bytes

# plans/M7.md item D, 03-hardware.md §3, `DmaShared[P, L]`'s own second
# sentence: "It **cannot be read as bytes** or lent as a plain value."
#
# A `@layout` field is exactly a byte view — declaring one as
# `DmaShared[P, L]` asks the compiler to say which bytes shared control
# memory *is*, which is the thing that sentence rules out. Permanent, not
# a fail-closed floor: no later item makes shared control memory
# describable as bytes. The fix is in the message — name the control
# structure's own `@layout(dma)` type as `L`.

@layout(dma, endian=little)
struct RingControl:
    flags: u16
    idx: u16

pool BlockControl

@layout(dma, endian=little)
struct Descriptor:
    ring: DmaShared[BlockControl, RingControl]
